    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d386">

                <pb facs="0385" n="269" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg269"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 822.00/340.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Consul General
                        Goding.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-02-14T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 14, 1914, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your February 13, 10 a.m. Department desires reports regarding revolution in the
                    north or possible revolutionary movement in Guayaquil when, in your judgment,
                    these are important. Press reports defeat of two thousand Government troops in
                    Manabi. Do you confirm this?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moore</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
